  "visual_differences": {
    "shared": "Native fonts, tighter tracking in the uppercase labels, HUD sizes and bar ends, opacity, and panel/button corners differ from the prototype. Coins, trust and the locked feature wording and order match the pictured states.",
    "w01": "Map marker rings, label outlines, gate shape and toolbar text-width spacing follow the live map. The longer bar overlaps more of the decorative canal label.",
    "w02–w05": "The live Weaver's lane uses greybox geometry and visible Layla capsule and label through the panel. The two-column Buy buttons are slightly wider and some status baselines and panel edges differ by a few pixels.",
    "w06–w09": "The same live lane, capsule and label show behind the wardrobe. Native text tracking, row-rule widths, and small button and panel offsets differ. A wardrobe with more outfits can scroll while Back stays visible.",
    "w10": "The live Spice row has greybox geometry and player and Rashid capsules. The stall panel covers part of Rashid's label.",
    "w11–w15": "The same Spice row backdrop shows Rashid's label above the panel. The native reputation panel is a little shorter and the primary button is wider. On w12 the Friday HUD at Spice row says Dhuhr under LOCK 2 while the Friday outfit line appears."
  },
